      "writtenOn": "2017-08-24T19:55:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Not at the moment. It just seemed more useful to me for the api to be \"we respect the flag that you pass\" rather than \"we set the flag to false for you\", partially to keep its usage clear (\"why would the flag exist if it gets ignored?\") and partially to avoid having to make a number of methods equal to 2^(number of flags we could want to set).\n\nWhat would be the advantage in calling it \"CreateHeaderWithoutDataDescriptor\"? Also, would we want that function to set the flag to false?\n\nI was also thinking about calling this new function CreateHeaderV2 , although I wasn\u0027t sure if that would someday conflict if the Go authors happened to make a function called CreateHeaderV2.",
      "parentUuid": "3db48af0_143b849e",
      "revId": "5811bfc13a9c7e49906ebf0f95c0cb682ac4fbdf",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9eda06ee_8700c55b",
        "filename": "cmd/soong_zip/soong_zip.go",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 363,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002751
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-08-24T20:02:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "My only concern with CreateHeaderAndroid is that switching a call from CreateHeader to CreateHeaderAndroid, with no changes to the flags, causes it to stop inserting the data descriptor.  Consider the case where we add another new flag.  If you switch CreateHeader to CreateHeaderAndroid and set the new flag, you are also unintentionally disabling data descriptors.\n\nWe could invert the meaning of the dataDescriptorFlag, maybe add a zip.JarCompatible flag instead, but it would mean the flags no longer had a 1-to-1 correspondence to the bits that end up in the zip file.",
      "parentUuid": "5bfc7309_93ca95e5",
      "revId": "5811bfc13a9c7e49906ebf0f95c0cb682ac4fbdf",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "cdd2fa99_efbcf8d4",
        "filename": "cmd/soong_zip/soong_zip.go",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 363,
      "author": {
        "id": 1137668
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-08-24T20:25:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "My thought is that the fact that CreateHeader accepts a parameter that it ignores is a mistake in the api and that CreateHeaderAndroid wouldn\u0027t try to be api-compatible. I guess it could be said that a better solution would be to remove that flag from the input type entirely so the caller doesn\u0027t have to think about whether to use a data descriptor or not.\n\nWould you like it better if CreateHeaderAndroid specified to write a data descriptor if and only if the method was not equal to Store (and therefore ignored the value passed in by the caller)?\n\nAs long as nobody tries to use the Stored method on a file whose size is more than 32 bits (and I hope nobody would want to do that) then we shouldn\u0027t have to implement 64-bit handling.",
      "parentUuid": "9eda06ee_8700c55b",
      "revId": "5811bfc13a9c7e49906ebf0f95c0cb682ac4fbdf",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    }
